{"id": "CAT-CU-02", "kind": "CU", "context": "Catalog", "title": "Archive a product", "text": "A catalogue manager withdraws a published product; it stays readable for history.\n\n## Rules\n\nAlso applies: CAT-RM-001, CAT-RM-004 — the product leaves the catalogue listing.", "status": "specified", "level": null, "path": "docs/business/Catalog/usecases/CAT-CU-02-archive-product.md", "line": 1, "end": 14, "cites": ["CAT-RM-001", "CAT-RM-004"], "usecases": ["CAT-CU-02"], "handlers": ["ArchiveProductCommandHandler"], "cited_by": ["ADR-001", "CAT-D-001"], "contexts": ["Catalog"]}
{"id": "CAT-RM-003", "kind": "RM", "context": "Catalog", "title": "Only a published product can be archived", "text": "Outcome: `ProductNotPublishedException`", "status": "specified", "level": null, "path": "docs/business/Catalog/usecases/CAT-CU-02-archive-product.md", "line": 9, "end": 11, "cites": [], "usecases": ["CAT-CU-02"], "handlers": ["ArchiveProductCommandHandler"], "cited_by": [], "contexts": ["Catalog"]}
{"id": "CAT-CU-03", "kind": "CU", "context": "Catalog", "title": "Restore an archived product", "text": "A catalogue manager puts back on sale a product archived by mistake.\n\n## Rules\n\nAlso applies: CAT-RM-001, CAT-RM-004 — the product reappears in the catalogue listing.", "status": "specified", "level": null, "path": "docs/business/Catalog/usecases/CAT-CU-03-restore-product.md", "line": 1, "end": 14, "cites": ["CAT-RM-001", "CAT-RM-004"], "usecases": ["CAT-CU-03"], "handlers": ["RestoreProductCommandHandler"], "cited_by": ["ADR-001", "CAT-D-001"], "contexts": ["Catalog"]}
{"id": "CAT-RM-005", "kind": "RM", "context": "Catalog", "title": "Only an archived product can be restored", "text": "Outcome: `ProductNotArchivedException`", "status": "specified", "level": null, "path": "docs/business/Catalog/usecases/CAT-CU-03-restore-product.md", "line": 9, "end": 11, "cites": [], "usecases": ["CAT-CU-03"], "handlers": ["RestoreProductCommandHandler"], "cited_by": [], "contexts": ["Catalog"]}
{"id": "ADR-001", "kind": "ADR", "context": null, "title": "Soft archive through a status column", "text": "Choice: `Product.Status = Archived`; listing queries filter on it.\nWhy: one read path, history preserved (CAT-D-001).\nRejected: archive table (two read paths); event-sourced projection (no event store).\nConsequences: every catalogue query filters on `Status`; index on (OrganisationId, Status).\nLinks: CAT-RM-004, CAT-CU-02, CAT-CU-03", "status": "specified", "level": null, "path": "docs/business/adr/ADR-001-soft-archive-through-a-status-column.md", "line": 1, "end": 7, "cites": ["CAT-CU-02", "CAT-CU-03", "CAT-D-001", "CAT-RM-004"], "usecases": ["CAT-CU-02", "CAT-CU-03"], "handlers": ["ArchiveProductCommandHandler", "RestoreProductCommandHandler"], "cited_by": [], "contexts": ["Catalog"]}
